[1.5.3]
* Update golang:1.27.3-trixie Docker digest to 7b072c5

[1.5.2]
* Update golang Docker tag to v1.27.3

[1.5.1]
* Update cloudron/base Docker tag to v6.0.1

[1.5.0]
* Audit log has a search, a filter by type and pages
* Admin groups are set with PG_ADMIN_GROUP in /app/data/env.sh, one or more groups separated by commas. New installs have no admin group, existing installs keep postgres-admins
* Name fields explain the allowed characters and why a name is not accepted, capitals become lowercase
* Admin > Server shows the default value of each empty setting
* Fixed the upload form layout on phones and the account tooltip in the top bar

[1.4.0]
* New panel design: icon buttons with optional labels, settings in sheets, a bottom navigation bar on phones
* Snapshot, restore and import progress updates live, without reloading the page
* Failure mails are opt-in: each user turns them on in the account settings. Owners no longer get them automatically
* Admins can change selected PostgreSQL settings (max_connections, memory and timeouts) in Admin > Server
* Admin overview links to lists of all client connections and all snapshots

[1.3.0]
* Logins can use Cloudron app passwords instead of a generated password, created in the Cloudron profile (needs Cloudron 10.0.5 or newer)
* Copy buttons next to connection URLs and new passwords

[1.2.0]
* Email to the role owners when a snapshot, restore or import fails, admins can add addresses that get every failure
* Mail is sent over STARTTLS with the Cloudron mail server certificate verified
* Requires Cloudron 10.0.1 or newer

[1.1.0]
* Database sizes on My databases, a usage card on each database page with size, connections and snapshot totals
* Admin page shows total database and snapshot size, used space of the data volume and per-database usage

[1.0.1]
* Docker image is published on the GitHub Container Registry

[1.0.0]
* Initial version with PostgreSQL 18.6
* Remote access over TLS 1.3 with SCRAM-SHA-256, blocked until a network is added to the allowlist
* Admin panel with Cloudron login: roles, databases, allowed networks, audit log
* Roles are owned by Cloudron users and groups. Every owner has an own login, it is removed when the user is no longer an owner
* Owners can create databases up to a limit set by the admin
* Snapshots on demand and on a schedule, download as .dump or .sql, restore into a staging database that is swapped in
* Import of uploaded pg_dump archives with SHA-256 checks
* Progress display for snapshots, restores and imports
